A few decades ago, it was almost impossible to buy clothes and wear them for the first time every day. The price and the lack of large chains, being very accessible and attractive to the public, led us to make a more thoughtful decision when buying.
Remember, the fashion industry is the second most polluting industry after oil, and our planet cannot allow big brands to manufacture garments by the piece without considering the long-term impact on us. For this reason, some designers, shops and stylists have decided to get down to work, with sustainability and care for the environment as a standard.
In addition to buying sustainable clothing in some of the sites that we recommend below, you can save the environment by going to vintage shops, creative workshops or swapping or renting clothes in some applications that are already successful. There is no doubt that protecting the planet today and keeping up to date are not incompatible things.
The most important thing for this company is to think about the present to leave a good legacy for future generations. Lifegist buys Global Organic Textile Standard (GOTS) certified fabrics in Europe, and Madrid is where all the clothing is produced to avoid the carbon footprint of shipping.
Ecoalf has established itself as one of the most recognizable names in sustainable fashion in our country, even beyond our borders. Its creator, Javier Goyeneche, wanted to demonstrate with his clothing that it was possible to continue having great quality and good taste without abusing natural resources.
This brand is 100% committed to the environment. So much so that all their shoes are designed in Barcelona and are the work of artisans who work in a factory near Alicante, which allows them to constantly check working conditions and production quality.
As you can see, it is important to wear clothing that reduces environmental impact, since it is one of the industries that most pollutes the planet and is consumed the most on a daily basis. I hope that with this information you can learn more about the main sustainable brands that exist and what their lines of work are.
