Many times we say that water has healthy nutrients for life, so it is not necessary to purify it. But finding high concentrations of agricultural and industrial fertilizers in drinking water changed the whole picture.
Fertilizer runoff from farmland pollutes water from rivers, streams, and lakes all the way to the ocean. Fertilizers are rich in different nutrients needed by plant life, and the resulting fresh water upsets the natural balance of essential nutrients for aquatic plants.
Water pollution has devastating effects on the protection of the environment and the health of the planet. Some of the most important consequences of the different types of water pollution are: destruction of biodiversity, contamination of the food chain, including the spread of toxic substances to food and the scarcity of drinking water.
