These are the best tips to learn how to humidify the environment without a humidifier:
Spreading a damp towel on the back of a chair, headboard, or footboard is a great way to moisten the air in your room. Remember not to roll up the towel as it will create an unpleasant smell.
This advice is good, half a bucket of water is enough in the room, as close as possible to the head of the bed to reduce the existing dry air and breathe better at night. You can use a bucket of aromatherapy water and put 2 drops of essential oil of lavender in the water, this plant has properties that help you calm down and relax.
It is important to remember that plants need care, water as long as the soil is not too wet and know if the plants should be exposed to the sun or the shade.
By showering with the bathroom door open, you allow water vapor to spread through the air, humidifying the environment and making the use of warm water more efficient. In summer it is more difficult to shower with hot water, so a good trick is leave the shower running with hot water for a few minutes while the person dries or gets dressed.
