The laser tube cutting machine is equipped with a manual loader that presents the tube to the operator who must then place the tube into the machine and manually tighten the chuck. Combining all these processes into one machine saves time and cost when processing tubes in large batches yet the machines versatility allows the user to easily make prototypes or small batch production.
This laser tube cutter is also equipped with a full enclosureto ensure the operator is safe while the machine is active.
Automatic correction For the bent and deformed pipe, the automatic correction function can realize the segmented edge search, and automatically correct the deviation to find the center point of the curved pipe for cutting to ensure the cutting precision.
When cutting to the last part of the tube, the front chuck jaws are automatically opened, and the rear chuck jaws pass through the front chuck to reduce the cutting blind area.
