The density of canvas fabric is calculated in metric system, which refers to the number of warp and weft yarns arranged in one square inch. The density directly affects the physical and mechanical indexes of the fabric, such as appearance, handle, thickness, strength, folding resistance, air permeability, wear resistance and thermal insulation performance.
This method is suitable for regular weave fabrics with high density and small yarn count. Firstly, the fabric weave and the number of warp (weft) in its weave cycle are analyzed, and then multiplied by the number of weave cycles in 10cm, the product is the warp (weft) density.
Canvas is usually divided into thick canvas and thin canvas. In addition, there are rubber canvas, fire, radiation shielding canvas, paper machine canvas.
Canvas, also known as awning cloth, is usually woven with 4-7 strands of 58 gauge (10 British thread). The fabric is firm and folding, and has good waterproof performance.
