According to calculation, a cloth shopping bag must be used at least 131 times before it can be regarded as truly environmental protection. If the used disposable plastic bags are used to hold garbage, professional handbags are wholesale and customized, and used 173 times, it can have the same impact on the environment as disposable plastic bags.
Producing a thin plastic bag made of high density polyethylene (HDPE) is equivalent to producing 1.57 kg of carbon dioxide, the report said. A cloth bag needs to be reused 171 times to be equivalent to the carbon dioxide emission of a plastic bag.
Fashion chains such as Primark love to provide paper bags for customers, but the study found that using paper bags three times is equivalent to the environmental impact of disposable plastic bags, while daily use bags made of thick plastic need to be used four times. The research project “supermarket shopping bag life cycle assessment” studies the impact of six different shopping bags on the environment.
