Most of these hair donation collection centers are specialized in rebuilding wigs from natural hair. In this way they can be used for people who need it, especially those who have had cancer or are suffering from alopecia.
It is important know the centers where this donation is going to be made and feel comfortable and confident where it is going to be sent. In case you did not know, there are also centers that collect used wigs during chemotherapy treatment when cancer was present.
In some places they do allow dyes, but hair must be very healthy or it has to be an exclusive norm of the center. If possible does not have to be cut into layers, as it may not keep the necessary length.
Curly hair can also be donated, but it must be at least 25 inches long.
You cannot use products such as hairspray, gel or any hair fixative. It is important that the hair is completely dry before being cut and put in its corresponding bag, since it could become moldy or weak.
