Contact Us Proper Food Storage Is Important To Prevent Cross Contamination In The Refrigerator
Contaminated foods are usually caused by inappropriately washing chopping boards and other food processing equipment. When the foods are being processed, the temperatures go up to kill bacteria, but sometimes cross-contamination happens on the cooked food is caused by it’s stored together with some raw meats other things with bacteria.
c. Store your fruits and ready-to-eat products from the raw meats. It would be better to separately use a fridge for meat storage from other foods.
Prevention Of Cross-Contamination When Processing & Preparing Foods For Deli When the foods are being processed or prepared for deli, you still need to follow the instructions to handle, as there is still a chance of cross-contamination occurrence, even the foods have been stored properly before.
b. It’s recommended that you separately used cutting boards to differentiate between different types of food items you are going to process, including vegetables, raw meats, fishes, vegetables, and fruits. You can also separately use knives for cutting different foods to prevent cross-contamination.
Cross-contamination can be avoided as every type of food is kept isolated to each other to stay safe. Separately using different processing tools when handling different foods also prevent transfer of bacteria and disease-causing micro-organisms from contaminated foods to other in a storage area.
