Why Do You Need To Clean Your Commercial Refrigerator And How Often
Resist Foul Odour With long-term use of your refrigerator, the foul odor may be produced by the items stored in it, which include expired food or something that is contaminated by bacteria or mold, foul odor can be caused by many things that are spoiled in the fridge.
With prolonged use of the refrigerator, the dust and dirt built up on the condenser coils will lower the efficiency and increase power consumption, so it’s crucial to regularly clean the coils to provide an optional working condition for your unit. Use the vacuum cleaner to get the loose dirt and dust from the coils, and then use a wet towel to wipe away the excess on the surface.
For optimal performance, it would be better to clean the evaporator coils every 6 months, as the evaporator is accumulating frost and ice due to prolonged use. You need to remove the ice and use a specialized detergent to clean the surface of the coils.
Check the door gaskets every 6 months to see if it’s cracked or hardened, the gaskets will not perform well and need to be replaced if it is aging. Clean the gaskets with soap if it is dirty.
