News - Useful Tips For Organizing Your Commercial Refrigerator
Properly organize your refrigerator can maintain the integrity of your products, and prevent food spoilage that can cause waste and economic loss.
Improperly stored food is much more likely to lead to violation of health and safety regulations. Your store or restaurant might be punished or even shut down.
You can quickly know what items are out of stock and need to be restocked when everything has a specific storage position. You can save much time on searching items that you don’t know where are.
Including the date of manufacture and expiration, so that you can know which products are older and try to use them first. Make sure you organize your storage according to the information on the labels, which can help you save a lot of time and money for your business.
All foods and items have their expiry date, so maintaining their quality is very important for retail and catering businesses. When organizing your storage space, make sure that you keep following the principle of FIFO (abbreviation of First-In, First-Out), always notice the date codes on the package, try to store older items in front of newer ones.
Benefits Of Organizing Your Commercial Refrigerator Following the organization guidelines for your commercial refrigerator can help you optimally utilize the storage space, and make your customers and staff easier to find the items.
And properly organized refrigerator can help save a lot of time and money for your business. There are some different types of refrigeration equipment for your options, including glass door fridge, glass door freezer, multideck display fridge, island display fridge, and so on, you can choose the right types with the specific design to hold different types of your products.
