1. Material preparation: Put the pipe or pipe fittings in a flat position and put them on the butt joint machine, leaving enough cutting allowance of 10-20mm.
Heating: The butt joint temperature is generally between 210-230℃. The heating time of the heating plate is different in winter and summer.
Melting butt joint: It is the key to welding. The butt joint process should always be carried out under melting pressure, and the width of the crimping should be 2-4mm.
Cooling: Keep the docking pressure constant, and let the interface cool down slowly. The length of the cooling time is based on the hard curling of the hand and no heat.
The docking is complete: After cooling down, loosen the slips, remove the docking machine, and prepare for the next interface connection.
