Many are the users who wonder which is the best clothes to go to the gym.
The first thing to do when choosing clothes to go to the gym is to stop and think carefully. what it means to exercise.
5 Leave your accessories at the locker
In addition, we must also use it on the seat of the machines where we must sit or lean, to prevent sweat from causing us to lose grip and, incidentally, not to leave the machines wet.
If we talk about clothing that absorbs moisture, we have to talk about cotton. However, it is a very bad idea.
Although sportswear is not cheap, we should invest in sports fabrics designed to keep sweat away from our bodies. Sportswear are blends of polyester and fiber.
In addition, these fabrics are very comfortable as well as flexible, so we will avoid all kinds of chafing that, in the long run, can be a completely unjustified reason for leaving the gym.
If you just joined the gym with the primary motivation of losing weight, don't buy the clothes you'd like to wear in a few months. Forget tight clothes that make you look like a shapeless black pudding.
Clothing that is too small is not an option either, as it will restrict our movements. If our size is too tight, we can opt for one more size to be more comfortable and avoid problems with sizes that are too large or too tight.
Elastane offers us a greater margin of movement during exercise, providing a very comfortable fit without being tight.
Wearing the right clothes increases your self-confidence as it makes you think of success. When you feel good in what you wear, you will work harder and achieve more.
It also offers protection and prevents injuries. Compression clothing will help us recover faster by improving blood flow and maintaining its speed, making blood reach the heart faster.
Flip flops are for locker rooms. Wearing sports shoes provides us with adequate support and protection for our feet (imagine dropping a dumbbell on your feet).
In addition, it reduces the risk of injury, improves physical performance and prevents us from slipping if we step on a few drops of sweat from an unscrupulous person who has left a towel at home. Related article:
Although I think it goes without saying, just as it is not a good idea to work out in the gym with flip-flops, it is not a good idea to wear only socks. If the footwear you wear makes you chafe, wearing socks will only aggravate the problem.
If you usually wear rings, bracelets or chains in your day to day, these are not necessary in the gym. You are doing sports, you do not have to show yourself as you are or as you like to be seen.
Regarding the rings, if you are exercising muscle in the upper part of the body, this can end up with scratches as well as discomfort in the fingers.
