With spring in its first few weeks, it's important to start developing new eating habits to ensure we maintain agood health during these weeks of climate change.
Froman increased need for proteinto maintain muscle mass, to have good hydration to protect facial hair,the diet of men must be especially careful as the heat begins to increaseand the sun seems to become more intense. Please note the following:
3 Look for healthy snacks
5 Drink enough water
As we mentioned above,the average man requires a higher intake of nutrientsto function properly, especially when we exercise constantly. For example, while the diet of women ranges from 1.600 to 2.000 calories, that of men rangesfrom 2.000 to 2.500 calories.
However,as the heat rises, people become more likely to overeat, so it is common to see generalized weight gains. This is not only negative for our health, but also for our self-esteem, since it makes us reach the summer with several extra kilos.
seasonal products,especially fruits and vegetables, are the best we can buy because they have nutrients adapted to the climate of the moment. In the case of spring and summer it is much easier to find foods with a high liquid content, as well as essential vitamins for hot days.
As the days get hotter,our body begins to use more energy to perform routine activities, making it necessary to eat more frequently in order to feel good. Healthy snacks thus become an important complement to our day-to-day life, remaining even until the summer.
From including marine animals to our diet, toeat vegetable protein, are some strategies that we can carry out to limit the intake of saturated fats, while significantly increasing the absorption of nutrients such as vitamins, antioxidants and minerals.
Although many of the foods we eat in the spring have a lot of liquid, the truth is thatrising temperatures make it that much more important to drink extra water.
Spring is a showy season and good weather, however,for men it is necessary to take into account additional precautionsto make sure we keep our body working optimally at all times.
