When Shenzhou 13 returned to the live broadcast, the astronauts generally sat on chairs and were carried away by the staff. According to professionals, this is because astronauts stay in a weightless environment in space for a long time, which will lead to serious problems such as muscle atrophy due to the lack of muscle strength.
As my country’s longest resident astronauts in space, the three astronauts on the Shenzhou 13 spacecraft are also the most affected by the gravity-free environment of space in my country. After they landed, there were rescuers and flight crews immediately Surgeons accompany them to help them re-adapt to gravity.
Although the design concept of the zero-gravity office chair (providing effective support for the whole body to achieve a static support mode of the human body that reduces the influence of gravity) is exactly in line with the low-gravity mode required by the astronauts after their return, but the redesign is designed for the Shenzhou 13 spacecraft. They also spent nearly half a year on the “escort chair” that the astronauts sat on.
