With the development of the times, car air-conditioning has become a necessity in the car: today, let’s talk to friends about which air-conditioning refrigeration or heating is more fuel-intensive? The answer is refrigeration
When the car air conditioner is cooled, it costs more oil, because the power of the car air conditioner when it cools accounts for about 10% to 15% of the engine’s output power. In order to illustrate this problem in detail, I will draw conclusions by analyzing the working principles of air-conditioning heating and cooling.
First of all, the principle of air conditioning heating is to let the engine coolant flow into the heat exchanger, and then the heated air is blown into the car by the blower.
Therefore, we can say that when the car is heated in winter, its fuel consumption is very small, or basically negligible. Turn on the heater and press the A/C button, the fuel consumption will increase
The majority of automotive air conditioning compressor is driven by the engine, which is bound to result in increased fuel consumption and engine burden. In cold areas in the north, turning on warm air may increase fuel consumption
Because in the cold north, the temperature is relatively low, so when the car water temperature is lower than the set value, in order to maintain the working temperature of the engine, the car computer will increase the fuel injection volume to maintain the normal working temperature of the engine.
Therefore, in this case, turning on the warm air will really increase fuel consumption.
